# WHITELIST, not a blocklist.
#
# This directory is a working root that also contains 20-odd checked-out
# repositories and a large amount of one-off material generated while solving
# problems -- handoff notes, probe scripts, patched copies of other people's
# launch files, logs. Almost none of it is something this repository should
# carry, and a blocklist would let the next one through by default.
#
# So: everything is ignored, and the bootstrap is added back by name. If you
# add a file that belongs here, add it below too.

*

# --- the bootstrap itself --------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!README.md
!tari.bash
!dgpy_install.sh
!colcon_defaults.yaml
!container.repos
!sim.repos
!acq.repos
!hw.repos
!site.repos
!workspace.repos

# --- checks over the bootstrap ---------------------------------------------
# Static checks on the scripts above -- no target environment, no ROS, nothing
# installed:  python3 -m pytest test/
!test/
!test/test_install_policy.py
!test/test_script_robustness.py
!test/test_extension_portability.py
# These two run real git repositories and real Python in a tmpdir rather than
# only reading the scripts, but still need no network, no ROS and nothing
# installed.
!test/test_sources_resume.py
!test/test_env_repair.py


# --- the container ---------------------------------------------------------
# The image definitions and the lifecycle script are one unit and now live in
# one repository, imported as the `container` layer into <workspace>/container.
# Only the forwarding stub is tracked here, so that ./ros2_docker.sh works
# straight after cloning the bootstrap and says how to get the rest.
!ros2_docker.sh

# --- never ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by tari.bash --phase env, machine-specific by construction.
tari_setup.bash
